              "title": "Justify or replace the photo-only identification method",
              "objects": [
                {
                  "type": "plain-text",
                  "begin": 211,
                  "end": 266,
                  "value": "Justify or replace the photo-only identification method"
                }
              ],
              "todoKeyword": "TODO",
              "todoType": "todo",
              "tags": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "section",
                  "begin": 267,
                  "end": 875,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "quote-block",
                      "begin": 267,
                      "end": 568,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "begin": 281,
                          "end": 555,
                          "text": "The main concern with the guide is the photo-only identification approach. It relies on the reader's eye and the light of the moment, which does not seem appropriate for species that differ only by the underside of the leaf, compared to a traditional key with measurements.",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "plain-text",
                              "begin": 281,
                              "end": 554,
                              "value": "The main concern with the guide is the photo-only identification approach. It relies on the reader's eye and the light of the moment, which does not seem appropriate for species that differ only by the underside of the leaf, compared to a traditional key with measurements."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "quote-block",
                      "begin": 568,
                      "end": 693,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "begin": 582,
                          "end": 680,
                          "text": "Photo identification gives no agreement between readers (unconvinced that it is appropriate here)",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "type": "plain-text",
                              "begin": 582,
                              "end": 679,
                              "value": "Photo identification gives no agreement between readers (unconvinced that it is appropriate here)"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "begin": 693,
                      "end": 875,
                      "text": "Following the suggestion of the reviewer, we have added a measurement for every step of the key. We continue to believe photographs are the right way into the guide for beginners.",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "plain-text",
                          "begin": 693,
                          "end": 872,
                          "value": "Following the suggestion of the reviewer, we have added a measurement for every step of the key. We continue to believe photographs are the right way into the guide for beginners."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
